1098
00:48:03.600 --> 00:48:06.060
This was a fan catch by Ella W.
这是粉丝Ella W.发现的。

1099
00:48:06.360 --> 00:48:07.040
and Abby W.
还有Abby W.。

1100
00:48:07.300 --> 00:48:07.980
What'd you catch?
你们发现了什么？

1101
00:48:08.220 --> 00:48:08.480
The W's.
W开头的问题。

1102
00:48:08.580 --> 00:48:09.220
What'd you catch?
你发现了什么？

1103
00:48:09.220 --> 00:48:16.380
They said in Diversity Day, Michael wishes aloud that he had some pad thai because he loves pad thai.
他们说在“多元化日”那一集里，迈克尔大声说他想吃泰式炒河粉，因为他很爱吃。

1104
00:48:16.620 --> 00:48:18.280
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1105
00:48:18.620 --> 00:48:19.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1106
00:48:19.320 --> 00:48:20.360
Great catch.
发现得好。

1107
00:48:20.780 --> 00:48:27.740
So they wondered, has Michael been telling people that he loves pad thai for years and he's still never tried it?
所以他们就在想，迈克尔是不是多年来一直跟人说他爱吃泰式炒河粉，但其实他从来没吃过？

1108
00:48:27.740 --> 00:48:29.240
But that's also-
但这其实也……

1109
00:48:29.240 --> 00:48:29.360
It's possible.
有可能。

1110
00:48:29.660 --> 00:48:34.180
It's also believable that he thinks that maybe it makes him seem well-traveled or something.
而且很有可能他觉得这样会让他显得很有阅历之类的。

1111
00:48:34.520 --> 00:48:34.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1112
00:48:34.980 --> 00:48:35.240
Right?
对吧？

1113
00:48:35.900 --> 00:48:40.920
Jenna, after the scene, the expense report deleted Runner would have continued.
珍娜，在那场戏之后，关于报销单被删掉的那个梗本来会继续下去的。

1114
00:48:41.520 --> 00:48:46.220
Andy is determined to get an extension on his expense reports and goes to talk to Angela.
安迪决心要让他的报销单获得延期，于是去找安吉拉谈。

1115
00:48:47.620 --> 00:48:49.640
These expenses are legitimate.
这些开销都是合法的。

1116
00:48:50.060 --> 00:48:51.120
Which I denied.
但我拒绝了。

1117
00:48:51.560 --> 00:48:51.940
Right.
没错。

1118
00:48:52.700 --> 00:48:55.960
Would you please respectfully reconsider these?
你能否郑重地重新考虑一下？

1119
00:48:56.280 --> 00:48:57.460
Why would I do that?
我为什么要那么做？

1120
00:48:57.560 --> 00:48:58.520
Because of our history.
因为我们的过去。

1121
00:48:59.320 --> 00:49:02.240
Both romantic and thrace-sexual.
既有浪漫史，也有两次性关系。

1122
00:49:04.000 --> 00:49:04.600
Twice.
两次。

1123
00:49:05.160 --> 00:49:07.140
I'd-
我……

1124
00:49:07.140 --> 00:49:09.040
Resubmit with proof of business.
重新提交，并附上业务证明。

1125
00:49:09.320 --> 00:49:12.640
Names of who you were with, what you talked about, phone numbers I can call to verify.
写上你和谁在一起，谈了什么，以及我可以拨打核实的电话号码。

1126
00:49:13.600 --> 00:49:16.880
You get a two-hour extension based on our history.
看在我们的过去，我给你两个小时的延期。

1127
00:49:17.600 --> 00:49:18.100
Right-o.
好嘞。

1128
00:49:18.640 --> 00:49:19.480
Then we're even.
那我们就扯平了。

1129
00:49:19.720 --> 00:49:20.040
Yeah.
是啊。

1130
00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:23.360
Wow.
哇。

1131
00:49:23.640 --> 00:49:24.420
I know.
我知道。

1132
00:49:25.620 --> 00:49:26.060
Hmm.
嗯。

1133
00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:27.480
Scandalous.
太离谱了。

1134
00:49:28.400 --> 00:49:29.480
Scandalous exchange.
真是离谱的对话。

1135
00:49:29.920 --> 00:49:33.520
So yes, Angela's going to give Andy a two-hour extension.
所以没错，安吉拉打算给安迪两个小时的延期。

1136
00:49:34.180 --> 00:49:35.920
What is he going to do with that?
他打算拿这段时间做什么？

1137
00:49:36.100 --> 00:49:36.980
You'll see.
你会看到的。

1138
00:49:37.240 --> 00:49:37.840
Okay.
好的。

1139
00:49:38.120 --> 00:49:39.060
Oh, I'm so glad.
噢，我太高兴了。

1140
00:49:39.060 --> 00:49:40.100
I have the clip.
我有这段剪辑。

1141
00:49:40.360 --> 00:49:42.120
I'm glad that pays off.
很高兴这个梗有了后续。

1142
00:49:42.680 --> 00:49:45.320
Oh, I'm very sad this runner was deleted.
噢，我很难过这段戏被删了。

1143
00:49:45.660 --> 00:49:46.000
I know.
我知道。

1144
00:49:46.100 --> 00:49:46.880
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

1145
00:49:47.120 --> 00:49:52.040
Now we're going to find out that Dunder Mifflin is going to offer Michael Scott Paper Company
现在我们要发现邓德·米福林公司要向迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司

1146
00:49:52.040 --> 00:49:53.560
a buyout.
提出收购了。

1147
00:49:53.980 --> 00:49:54.460
Yes.
是的。

1148
00:49:54.760 --> 00:49:58.520
So Jim is going to go into Michael Scott Paper Company and give them this news.
所以吉姆要去迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司把这个消息告诉他们。

1149
00:49:58.800 --> 00:50:01.120
And Michael is like, what?
而迈克尔的反应是，什么？

1150
00:50:01.280 --> 00:50:02.420
Why would they want to do that?
他们为什么要这么做？

1151
00:50:02.560 --> 00:50:04.040
We're totally like broke.
我们简直穷得叮当响。

1152
00:50:04.040 --> 00:50:05.400
And Jim's like, I did it.
然后吉姆说，我搞定了。

1153
00:50:06.020 --> 00:50:08.580
Like, once I hear it, I can't unhear it.
就像是，一旦我听到了，就再也忘不掉了。

1154
00:50:08.660 --> 00:50:09.600
So don't say it.
所以别说出来。

1155
00:50:10.140 --> 00:50:12.240
And so Michael gets it.
然后迈克尔明白了。

1156
00:50:12.500 --> 00:50:17.500
Steve has another one of those amazing moments where he comes to a realization very slowly.
史蒂夫又贡献了一个精彩瞬间，他非常缓慢地领悟到了这一点。

1157
00:50:17.780 --> 00:50:21.060
The three of them are going to go upstairs now to meet.
他们三个人现在要上楼去开会了。

1158
00:50:21.980 --> 00:50:27.340
And Ryan and Pam are like, Michael, you cannot say that we are broke.
瑞安和帕姆就说，迈克尔，你不能说我们破产了。

1159
00:50:27.500 --> 00:50:28.880
You cannot do it.
你不能这么做。

1160
00:50:28.960 --> 00:50:29.820
Are we clear?
听清楚了吗？

1161
00:50:29.820 --> 00:50:32.440
We are not going to mention that we are broke.
我们绝不能提我们破产的事。

1162
00:50:32.560 --> 00:50:33.300
And he's like, I got it.
然后他说，我明白了。

1163
00:50:33.360 --> 00:50:33.720
I got it.
我明白了。

1164
00:50:33.720 --> 00:50:37.120
They get in the elevator, the door's open on the next floor.
他们进了电梯，门在下一层打开了。

1165
00:50:37.140 --> 00:50:38.180
And he's like, I don't got it.
然后他说，我没明白。

1166
00:50:38.300 --> 00:50:39.460
I can't do it.
我做不到。

1167
00:50:39.600 --> 00:50:40.740
I loved it so much.
我太喜欢这一段了。

1168
00:50:40.760 --> 00:50:41.840
It made me laugh out loud.
它让我大笑出声。

1169
00:50:42.100 --> 00:50:44.920
That's a whole fakie elevator, as everyone knows.
众所周知，那整个电梯都是假的。

1170
00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:46.200
We got in the elevator.
我们进了电梯。

1171
00:50:46.360 --> 00:50:52.380
The guy with the pulleys pulled the rope, shut the doors, and then we relocated to a
那个拉滑轮的人拉动绳子，关上门，然后我们被转移到了

1172
00:50:52.380 --> 00:50:56.120
completely different building, to the Dunder Mifflin elevator.
另一栋完全不同的建筑里，到了邓德·米夫林的电梯。

1173
00:50:56.720 --> 00:50:58.900
And we got out, and it is seamless.
我们走出来，衔接得天衣无缝。

1174
00:50:59.040 --> 00:51:00.560
It looks so good.
看起来太棒了。

1175
00:51:01.060 --> 00:51:02.600
Ugh, that was funny.
天哪，那太搞笑了。

1176
00:51:02.600 --> 00:51:10.320
And then we walk in, and Michael has his line that I have seen quoted so many times, where
然后我们走进去，迈克尔说了那句我见过无数人引用的台词，他说，

1177
00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:15.800
he says, well, well, well, how the turntables.
好吧，好吧，好吧，风水轮流转啊（how the turntables）。

1178
00:51:17.580 --> 00:51:20.800
Okay, I had to know how that was scripted.
好吧，我必须得知道那句台词是怎么写的。

1179
00:51:20.800 --> 00:51:24.720
So I went to the shooting draft, and that line is not in the script.
所以我去看了拍摄剧本，那句台词根本不在剧本里。

1180
00:51:25.020 --> 00:51:27.940
Oh my gosh, we got a fan question about that.
天哪，我们收到过关于这个的粉丝提问。

1181
00:51:28.200 --> 00:51:30.900
Yeah, I don't know if it was pitched on the fly.
是啊，我不知道那是现场想出来的，

1182
00:51:30.900 --> 00:51:34.900
You know how sometimes writers would have some pitches, or if Steve improvised it.
你知道有时候编剧会有些点子，或者是不是史蒂夫即兴发挥的。

1183
00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:36.120
I don't know.
我不知道。

1184
00:51:36.240 --> 00:51:38.480
But in the script, this is what it said.
但在剧本里，原文是这样的。

1185
00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:40.080
Well, well, well.
好吧，好吧，好吧。

1186
00:51:40.360 --> 00:51:42.360
Oh, how the meteors fallen.
噢，流星陨落了（how the meteors fallen）。

1187
00:51:43.060 --> 00:51:43.400
Hmm.
嗯。

1188
00:51:43.400 --> 00:51:46.540
And I love the turntables so much better.
我还是觉得“风水轮流转”（turntables）好得多。

1189
00:51:47.920 --> 00:51:49.440
Turntables is so funny.
“风水轮流转”太搞笑了。

1190
00:51:49.620 --> 00:51:50.200
I know.
我知道。

1191
00:51:50.500 --> 00:51:53.040
Because Michael gets all of his phrases slightly off.
因为迈克尔总是把所有的成语说得稍微有点偏差。

1192
00:51:53.120 --> 00:51:53.960
And Michael, you know what?
而且迈克尔，你知道吗？

1193
00:51:54.020 --> 00:51:55.160
I can relate to that.
我对此深有同感。

1194
00:51:56.240 --> 00:51:57.360
And you still sell-
你还是会卖——

1195
00:51:57.360 --> 00:51:57.980
Frider Day.
星期五（Frider Day）。

1196
00:51:58.300 --> 00:51:59.040
Frider Day.
星期五（Frider Day）。

1197
00:51:59.320 --> 00:52:01.120
For years, I've been saying Frider Day.
多年来，我一直把星期五说成“Frider Day”。

1198
00:52:01.200 --> 00:52:02.420
I've been saying lots of things.
我一直都在说错很多东西。

1199
00:52:04.140 --> 00:52:09.640
I love that when they get into the conference room, Michael immediately rejects their first
我喜欢当他们进入会议室时，迈克尔立刻拒绝了他们的第一个

1200
00:52:09.640 --> 00:52:12.320
offer, and he says, just give me your second offer.
报价，他说，直接给我你们的第二个报价吧。

1201
00:52:12.780 --> 00:52:13.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1202
00:52:13.480 --> 00:52:16.520
And their second offer is a buyout of $12,000.
他们的第二个报价是12000美元的买断费。

1203
00:52:17.640 --> 00:52:22.720
Kelly and Angela are trying to eavesdrop, and Kelly has her ear to the door with like
凯莉和安吉拉试图偷听，凯莉把耳朵贴在门上，还拿着个

1204
00:52:22.720 --> 00:52:23.720
a coffee mug.
咖啡杯。

1205
00:52:24.100 --> 00:52:25.420
Mindy and I kept laughing.
明迪和我一直在笑。

1206
00:52:25.680 --> 00:52:26.760
That was so funny.
那太好笑了。

1207
00:52:26.920 --> 00:52:28.460
It was so ridiculous.
简直荒谬透顶。

1208
00:52:28.460 --> 00:52:31.420
We're so invested in what Charles is doing.
我们太关注查尔斯在做什么了。

1209
00:52:31.420 --> 00:52:33.580
We have to be eavesdropping.
我们必须得偷听。

1210
00:52:33.780 --> 00:52:36.820
And you know, I remember Mindy tried a few different things.
你知道，我记得明迪试过几种不同的演法。

1211
00:52:37.060 --> 00:52:40.200
In the script, I asked Kelly, what do you hear?
剧本里，我问凯莉，你听到了什么？

1212
00:52:40.300 --> 00:52:43.200
And she actually responds and says, the ocean.
她真的回答说，听到了大海的声音。

1213
00:52:43.560 --> 00:52:43.880
Oh.
噢。

1214
00:52:44.200 --> 00:52:48.880
But in the episode, we have this wah, wah, wah, wah, wah, wah, wah, wah, wah, wah.
但在正片里，我们用了那种哇、哇、哇、哇、哇、哇、哇、哇、哇、哇的声音。

1215
00:52:49.080 --> 00:52:50.460
She was so good at it.
她演得太棒了。

1216
00:52:50.600 --> 00:52:52.400
She was doing Charlie Brown's teacher, right?
她在模仿查理·布朗老师的声音，对吧？

1217
00:52:52.400 --> 00:52:53.440
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1218
00:52:53.440 --> 00:52:54.440
We were tickled.
我们都乐坏了。

1219
00:52:54.720 --> 00:52:58.160
Well, Michael is going to reject this offer of $12,000.
迈克尔打算拒绝这12000美元的报价。

1220
00:52:58.760 --> 00:53:03.020
And this is when he is a brilliant negotiator.
这就是他展现谈判天才的时候。

1221
00:53:03.280 --> 00:53:05.220
I could not believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

1222
00:53:05.400 --> 00:53:06.840
Do you see the look on Pam's face?
你看到帕姆脸上的表情了吗？

1223
00:53:06.920 --> 00:53:07.400
I do.
看到了。

1224
00:53:07.560 --> 00:53:09.300
Pam is all of us in this moment.
这一刻的帕姆就是我们所有人的写照。

1225
00:53:09.760 --> 00:53:10.280
Exactly.
没错。

1226
00:53:10.780 --> 00:53:15.840
So he gets David to give them an offer of $60,000.
所以他让大卫给他们开出了6万美元的报价。

1227
00:53:16.500 --> 00:53:16.840
Yes.
是的。

1228
00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:19.320
He's like, listen, here's how I see it.
他说，听着，我是这么看的。

1229
00:53:19.440 --> 00:53:21.220
You're up for approval by the board.
你正等着董事会的批准。

1230
00:53:21.380 --> 00:53:21.740
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1231
00:53:21.740 --> 00:53:25.980
And they're probably not going to be too happy that you are losing customers to Michael
他们可能不会太高兴看到你正在流失客户给迈克尔·斯科特

1232
00:53:25.980 --> 00:53:26.920
Scott Paper Company.
造纸公司。

1233
00:53:27.140 --> 00:53:27.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1234
00:53:27.520 --> 00:53:29.740
So you actually need me.
所以你其实需要我。

1235
00:53:30.220 --> 00:53:30.580
Yes.
没错。

1236
00:53:30.960 --> 00:53:33.760
So they say, we'll give you a moment to discuss it.
于是他们说，给你一点时间商量一下。

1237
00:53:33.820 --> 00:53:37.580
And now we're going to have a scene out at Dwight and Jim's desks.
现在我们要转到德怀特和吉姆办公桌那边的场景了。

1238
00:53:37.740 --> 00:53:39.440
But did you notice behind them?
但你注意到他们身后了吗？

1239
00:53:39.760 --> 00:53:42.560
No one is in the conference room and the door is open.
会议室里没人，而且门是开着的。

1240
00:53:42.800 --> 00:53:44.520
It's a total continuity catch.
这是一个明显的连贯性失误。

1241
00:53:45.140 --> 00:53:48.780
Ryan, Michael, and Pam should have been in the background there.
瑞安、迈克尔和帕姆本应该出现在背景里的。

1242
00:53:48.780 --> 00:53:49.920
And they're not.
但他们不在。

1243
00:53:50.300 --> 00:53:51.700
Oh, good catch.
噢，观察得很仔细。

1244
00:53:52.120 --> 00:53:52.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1245
00:53:52.920 --> 00:53:59.420
But Dwight gets this phone call from a client saying that Michael Scott Paper Company called
但德怀特接到了一个客户的电话，说迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司打电话

1246
00:53:59.420 --> 00:54:03.300
them and asked them for more money and they'd like to come back to Dunder Mifflin.
向他们要更多的钱，他们想回到邓德·米夫林。

1247
00:54:03.580 --> 00:54:06.240
And Dwight's going to run into the kitchen and tattle.
德怀特跑进厨房去告密了。

1248
00:54:06.420 --> 00:54:09.080
He's going to tell Charles, Michael Scott Paper Company is going broke.
他要去告诉查尔斯，迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司快破产了。

1249
00:54:09.280 --> 00:54:14.180
And normally Charles would take that information from Dwight and go right into action.
通常情况下，查尔斯会采纳德怀特的情报并立即采取行动。

1250
00:54:14.200 --> 00:54:17.160
But Dwight's been acting so strange to Charles all day.
但德怀特今天一整天对查尔斯的表现都太奇怪了。

1251
00:54:17.160 --> 00:54:19.780
And then Jim capitalizes on that.
然后吉姆就利用了这一点。

1252
00:54:20.200 --> 00:54:20.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1253
00:54:20.540 --> 00:54:28.780
He kind of baits Dwight into bringing out his full weirdo by sort of heckling him about
他有点像是在诱导德怀特，通过嘲讽他，

1254
00:54:28.780 --> 00:54:30.600
his ability to solve cases.
让他彻底暴露自己的怪胎本性，去证明他破案的能力。

1255
00:54:30.720 --> 00:54:32.560
And Charles is like, you're both morons.
而查尔斯觉得，你们俩都是白痴。

1256
00:54:32.560 --> 00:54:34.700
Don't go anywhere near the conference room.
别靠近会议室半步。

1257
00:54:35.040 --> 00:54:38.320
Here's what I need to bring up about this scene on a practical level.
关于这场戏，我得从实际操作层面提一点。

1258
00:54:38.460 --> 00:54:41.260
Did you notice where Charles is standing in this scene?
你注意到查尔斯在这场戏里站的位置了吗？

1259
00:54:41.580 --> 00:54:42.340
By the counter?
在柜台旁边？

1260
00:54:42.720 --> 00:54:43.200
Yes.
没错。

1261
00:54:43.360 --> 00:54:44.820
But very close to the fridge.
但离冰箱非常近。

1262
00:54:44.820 --> 00:54:49.540
And through the entire scene, he's got his Sadekoy steel coffee mug.
而且整场戏里，他都拿着那个萨德科伊钢制咖啡杯。

1263
00:54:49.680 --> 00:54:50.000
Yeah.
是啊。

1264
00:54:50.140 --> 00:54:52.420
And he's got a full coffee pot.
手里还提着一整壶咖啡。

1265
00:54:52.620 --> 00:54:54.640
Each hand is holding one of these iteMs.
两只手各拿着一样东西。

1266
00:54:55.200 --> 00:55:02.160
Why did he walk so far away from the coffee maker to put his coffee in his mug?
他为什么要走那么远，离开咖啡机去往杯子里倒咖啡？

1267
00:55:02.280 --> 00:55:05.740
Because the coffee maker is over by the door that leads to the office.
因为咖啡机在通往办公室的那扇门旁边。

1268
00:55:06.040 --> 00:55:10.340
So this man is saddled with these two coffee iteMs.
所以这个男人被这两样咖啡用品给困住了。

1269
00:55:10.480 --> 00:55:12.380
And I'm just like, why did he drift?
我当时就在想，他为什么要走开？

1270
00:55:12.380 --> 00:55:17.620
In my mind as an actor, I'm having to make up a reason why this happened.
作为演员，我得在脑子里编个理由来解释为什么会这样。

1271
00:55:17.760 --> 00:55:23.180
So I'm imagining he got the coffee pot and he's starting to pour and he notices something
所以我脑补他拿到了咖啡壶，刚开始倒咖啡，就注意到了

1272
00:55:23.180 --> 00:55:23.820
on the fridge.
冰箱上的什么东西。

1273
00:55:23.960 --> 00:55:25.480
He wants to get a closer look.
他想凑近看一看。

1274
00:55:25.800 --> 00:55:30.580
And then Dwight comes in and he's now stuck with his two coffees.
然后德怀特进来了，他就被这两杯咖啡给困住了。

1275
00:55:30.800 --> 00:55:31.620
I don't know.
我不知道。

1276
00:55:31.780 --> 00:55:33.540
It was an odd staging for me.
对我来说这调度很奇怪。

1277
00:55:33.680 --> 00:55:34.880
And I became distracted.
我当时就走神了。

1278
00:55:35.240 --> 00:55:37.940
I love that like this moment pulled you out for a minute.
我喜欢这种时刻，它让你出戏了一会儿。

1279
00:55:38.120 --> 00:55:40.800
Like as an actor process, you're like, that makes no sense.
就像作为演员，你会觉得这完全不合逻辑。

1280
00:55:40.800 --> 00:55:42.180
I'm like, I need a reason.
我当时就在想，我需要一个理由。

1281
00:55:42.440 --> 00:55:43.760
I need a motivation.
我需要一个动机。

1282
00:55:44.320 --> 00:55:49.620
Back in the conference room, Michael says no to this very lucrative offer.
回到会议室，迈克尔拒绝了这份非常丰厚的提议。

1283
00:55:49.880 --> 00:55:50.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1284
00:55:50.280 --> 00:55:52.160
And Pam is like, can we have another minute?
帕姆说，我们能再商量一下吗？

1285
00:55:52.440 --> 00:55:52.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1286
00:55:52.940 --> 00:55:56.400
And this is when Michael, again, makes perfect sense.
就在这时，迈克尔再次展现了他极其理智的一面。

1287
00:55:56.400 --> 00:55:59.260
And he says, what we need are jobs.
他说，我们需要的是工作。

1288
00:55:59.520 --> 00:56:01.000
We don't need a buyout.
我们不需要买断费。

1289
00:56:01.160 --> 00:56:02.560
That money's not going to last forever.
那笔钱花不了多久的。

1290
00:56:02.720 --> 00:56:03.540
We need employment.
我们需要的是就业。

1291
00:56:03.540 --> 00:56:04.780
And everyone agrees.
大家都表示赞同。

1292
00:56:05.100 --> 00:56:05.320
Yes.
没错。

1293
00:56:05.420 --> 00:56:07.340
This is his teach a man to fish moment.
这就是他“授人以渔”的高光时刻。

1294
00:56:07.460 --> 00:56:07.940
Yes.
没错。

1295
00:56:08.080 --> 00:56:08.300
Right?
对吧？

1296
00:56:08.300 --> 00:56:11.980
So when they come back in, that's what Michael is going to say.
所以当他们回来时，迈克尔要说的就是这个。

1297
00:56:12.100 --> 00:56:14.040
You have to hire all of us back.
你们必须把我们所有人都雇回去。

1298
00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:18.120
And also, in addition to jobs, Michael wants his Sebring again.
而且除了工作，迈克尔还想要回他的赛百灵轿车。

1299
00:56:18.320 --> 00:56:19.640
And his old parking space.
还有他原来的停车位。

1300
00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:23.420
But Charles says they don't make Sebrings anymore.
但查尔斯说赛百灵已经停产了。

1301
00:56:23.940 --> 00:56:24.980
Is that true?
那是真的吗？

1302
00:56:25.440 --> 00:56:27.360
Lady, you know I had to know.
女士，你知道我必须得弄清楚。

1303
00:56:27.540 --> 00:56:31.820
Oh, I'm so glad you looked this up because I didn't look it up and it has been bothering me.
噢，我真高兴你查了这个，因为我没查，这事一直困扰着我。

1304
00:56:31.940 --> 00:56:32.360
All right.
好吧。

1305
00:56:32.720 --> 00:56:33.820
Charles is wrong.
查尔斯错了。

1306
00:56:34.120 --> 00:56:36.200
They are still making the Sebring.
他们还在生产赛百灵。

1307
00:56:36.200 --> 00:56:39.340
This episode aired April of 2009.
这一集是在2009年4月播出的。

1308
00:56:39.640 --> 00:56:46.460
According to the internet, they made the Chrysler Sebring from 1995 to 2010.
根据互联网上的信息，克莱斯勒赛百灵的生产年份是1995年到2010年。

1309
00:56:47.030 --> 00:56:52.780
And in looking up this fact, I ended up watching several Sebring commercials over the years.
在查证这个事实的过程中，我顺便看了好几个这些年来的赛百灵广告。

1310
00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:53.560
Oh.
噢。

1311
00:56:54.100 --> 00:56:56.820
You really were infested.
你真是中毒太深了。

1312
00:56:57.040 --> 00:57:00.200
I think I watched half an hour worth of commercials.
我想我看了足足半小时的广告。

1313
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:02.720
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1314
00:57:02.900 --> 00:57:05.480
They made some really interesting choices in their commercials.
他们的广告里做了一些非常有趣的选角。

1315
00:57:05.840 --> 00:57:08.080
But there's one I really needed you to hear.
但有一个广告我真的得让你听听。

1316
00:57:08.420 --> 00:57:09.860
It is from 1995.
那是1995年的。

1317
00:57:10.220 --> 00:57:12.080
It's the year the car debuted.
那是这款车首次亮相的年份。

1318
00:57:12.480 --> 00:57:14.900
Can we please play that Sebring commercial?
我们能播放一下那个赛百灵广告吗？

1319
00:57:15.580 --> 00:57:20.480
The new Chrysler Sebring was built upon something called the Goldilocks principle.
新款克莱斯勒赛百灵是基于所谓的“金发姑娘原则”打造的。

1320
00:57:20.880 --> 00:57:25.720
It occurred to us that while most luxury cars were too big, most sport coupes were too small.
我们意识到，大多数豪华轿车太大了，而大多数运动轿跑车又太小了。

1321
00:57:26.040 --> 00:57:29.700
We wanted the Sebring to be, well, just right.
我们想让赛百灵做到，嗯，恰到好处。

1322
00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:38.300
It not only has a sporty 24-valve engine and a race-inspired suspension, but it also gives you the luxury of an actual backseat.
它不仅拥有运动型的24气门发动机和赛车级悬挂系统，还为你提供了真正后排座椅的豪华感。

1323
00:57:38.500 --> 00:57:40.840
Which means there's enough room for Goldilocks.
这意味着它有足够的空间容纳金发姑娘。

1324
00:57:41.060 --> 00:57:43.320
And three or four of our friends.
还有她的三四个朋友。

1325
00:57:45.340 --> 00:57:50.170
I have to say, okay, so Sam is not with us this week.
我得说，好吧，山姆这周不在我们身边。

1326
00:57:50.330 --> 00:57:50.910
He's on vacation.
他在度假。

1327
00:57:51.150 --> 00:57:52.210
Jordan is filling in.
乔丹来代班。

1328
00:57:52.310 --> 00:57:54.070
And it is like laughing.
她笑得不行了。

1329
00:57:54.310 --> 00:57:57.570
I can see her laughing at that commercial.
我能看到她在看那个广告时笑得样子。

1330
00:57:58.190 --> 00:57:58.830
Thank you, guys.
谢谢你们。

1331
00:57:59.250 --> 00:58:04.030
When watching my half an hour of Chrysler commercials for the Sebring, I'd had a glass of wine.
当我看了半小时克莱斯勒赛百灵的广告时，我刚好喝了一杯红酒。

1332
00:58:04.490 --> 00:58:07.930
And when we got to this one, I literally did a spit take.
当看到这个广告时，我简直把酒喷了出来。

1333
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:08.910
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么鬼？

1334
00:58:09.570 --> 00:58:12.170
And the whole time the car is driving through the woods.
而且整段广告里车都在树林里穿行。

1335
00:58:12.670 --> 00:58:13.110
Okay.
好吧。

1336
00:58:13.450 --> 00:58:14.570
Oh, because of Goldilocks.
噢，因为金发姑娘嘛。

1337
00:58:14.570 --> 00:58:15.530
And the three bears.
还有三只熊。

1338
00:58:15.710 --> 00:58:15.850
Yeah.
没错。

1339
00:58:16.090 --> 00:58:18.710
But when they were like, to fit a few of her friends.
但当他们说“容纳她的几个朋友”时。

1340
00:58:19.110 --> 00:58:19.930
It was over.
我彻底笑喷了。

1341
00:58:22.980 --> 00:58:23.500
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1342
00:58:23.520 --> 00:58:24.320
I had to share that.
我一定要分享这个。

1343
00:58:24.480 --> 00:58:26.340
So, yes, they still had the Sebring.
所以，没错，他们当时还在生产赛百灵。

1344
00:58:26.460 --> 00:58:29.600
They could have given Michael a Sebring in April of 2009.
他们在2009年4月完全可以给迈克尔一辆赛百灵。

1345
00:58:30.200 --> 00:58:36.220
By the way, I want to say, you know my friend Stacy, who I invented the tan baster with?
顺便说一下，我想说，你认识我那个一起发明了美黑喷雾的朋友史黛西吗？

1346
00:58:36.480 --> 00:58:36.880
Yes.
认识。

1347
00:58:36.880 --> 00:58:38.180
She drove a Sebring.
她开的就是赛百灵。

1348
00:58:38.340 --> 00:58:38.800
She drove a Sebring.
她开的就是赛百灵。

1349
00:58:38.800 --> 00:58:38.850
Oh.
噢。

1350
00:58:39.040 --> 00:58:40.420
And it was a lovely car.
那是一辆很棒的车。

1351
00:58:40.420 --> 00:58:44.100
I have to say, it was kind of like, they're right.
我不得不说，感觉就像他们说的那样。

1352
00:58:44.260 --> 00:58:49.480
It was a really nice combination of a sporty coupe, but also roomy.
它完美结合了运动轿跑的风格，但空间又很宽敞。

1353
00:58:49.660 --> 00:58:50.900
But with a comfortable backseat.
而且后座很舒服。

1354
00:58:51.140 --> 00:58:51.760
I don't know.
我不知道。

1355
00:58:51.820 --> 00:58:52.920
I never sat in the backseat.
我从没坐过那个后座。

1356
00:58:52.920 --> 00:58:55.060
Well, Goldilocks would have been happy with it.
嗯，金发姑娘肯定会很满意。

1357
00:58:55.080 --> 00:58:56.080
She could have sat back there.
她完全可以坐在后面。

1358
00:58:56.840 --> 00:59:02.760
Also, since we brought up Jordan, Jordan did our song parody, Total Eclipse of the Fart.
另外，既然提到了乔丹，乔丹还翻唱了我们的恶搞歌曲《屁之全面日食》。

1359
00:59:03.020 --> 00:59:03.360
Yes.
没错。

1360
00:59:03.460 --> 00:59:04.900
That was Jordan who sang that.
那首歌就是乔丹唱的。

1361
00:59:05.080 --> 00:59:06.240
We're very happy to have you.
很高兴你能来。

1362
00:59:06.240 --> 00:59:07.860
Thank you for filling in for Sam today.
谢谢你今天代班萨姆。

1363
00:59:08.160 --> 00:59:08.320
Yes.
是的。

1364
00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:11.200
Sam, I brought cake today, so you missed out on that.
萨姆，我今天带了蛋糕，你错过了。

1365
00:59:11.420 --> 00:59:13.660
I also got it on my sweater as I walked in.
我走进来的时候还弄到了毛衣上。

1366
00:59:13.940 --> 00:59:14.240
Yeah.
是啊。

1367
00:59:14.360 --> 00:59:16.420
I noticed it right away when you walked in.
你一走进来我就注意到了。

1368
00:59:16.520 --> 00:59:19.280
And I thought, I don't know, it's ketchup or something.
我还以为，不知道，是番茄酱还是什么的。

1369
00:59:19.540 --> 00:59:21.260
You thought I had a messy breakfaSt.
你以为我早餐吃得一团糟。

1370
00:59:21.560 --> 00:59:22.220
I guess I did.
我想确实是。

1371
00:59:22.220 --> 00:59:23.080
I guess I did.
我想确实是。

1372
00:59:23.200 --> 00:59:26.300
I thought it was leftover maybe from the last time you wore it.
我还以为那是你上次穿这件衣服留下的。

1373
00:59:26.380 --> 00:59:26.840
Jenna.
珍娜。

1374
00:59:27.220 --> 00:59:27.520
What?
怎么了？

1375
00:59:28.060 --> 00:59:32.640
I wouldn't leave food on my hoodie and hang it back up.
我才不会把食物留在卫衣上就直接挂起来呢。

1376
00:59:32.780 --> 00:59:34.840
If you didn't notice, you might.
如果你没注意到，说不定会。

1377
00:59:34.840 --> 00:59:37.080
Wait, have you never not noticed?
等等，你难道从来没有没注意到过吗？

1378
00:59:37.980 --> 00:59:40.120
It's a pretty big mark right on my boob.
那可是个很大的污渍，就在我胸口上。

1379
00:59:40.260 --> 00:59:43.100
I love that my husband, though, didn't say a word as I walked out.
不过我真没想到，我出门时我丈夫竟然一句话都没说。

1380
00:59:43.260 --> 00:59:44.280
Josh, come on.
乔什，拜托。

1381
00:59:44.840 --> 00:59:45.460
All right.
好吧。

1382
00:59:45.680 --> 00:59:47.400
So back to this episode.
回到这一集。

1383
00:59:47.600 --> 00:59:50.340
Would you like to hear how the expense report finished?
你们想听听费用报销单的后续吗？

1384
00:59:50.540 --> 00:59:51.060
Yes, please.
想，请讲。

1385
00:59:51.320 --> 00:59:56.140
Because in the script, this is where it would have wrapped up Angela and Andy,
因为在剧本里，这本该是安吉拉和安迪的结局，

1386
00:59:56.360 --> 00:59:59.000
their final scene about the expense report.
他们关于费用报销单的最后一场戏。

1387
01:00:00.100 --> 01:00:03.600
And now, with no further rid-a-dit-a-do,
现在，无需再多说废话，

1388
01:00:04.260 --> 01:00:05.680
my revised expense report.
这是我修改后的费用报销单。

1389
01:00:05.700 --> 01:00:06.100
The deadline's passed.
截止日期已经过了。

1390
01:00:06.100 --> 01:00:06.300
What?
什么？

1391
01:00:06.720 --> 01:00:07.080
When?
什么时候？

1392
01:00:07.300 --> 01:00:08.860
When you were saying rid-a-dit-a-do.
就在你说废话的时候。

1393
01:00:10.440 --> 01:00:12.420
It's rid-a-dit-a-do.
那是废话。

1394
01:00:12.560 --> 01:00:12.860
I know.
我知道。

1395
01:00:12.880 --> 01:00:14.080
I've always been such a fan of it.
我一直都很喜欢这个梗。

1396
01:00:18.350 --> 01:00:19.350
Oh, wow.
噢，哇。

1397
01:00:21.500 --> 01:00:21.900
Delicious?
好吃吗？

1398
01:00:22.640 --> 01:00:24.140
I'm really sad that got cut.
真遗憾这段被剪掉了。

1399
01:00:24.620 --> 01:00:25.540
Me, too.
我也是。

1400
01:00:25.920 --> 01:00:28.040
Oh, and as soon as he was like,
噢，他一说，

1401
01:00:28.580 --> 01:00:30.880
I just turn around and I don't look at him anymore,
我只要转过身，不再看他，

1402
01:00:30.880 --> 01:00:32.120
and he has to walk away.
他就只能走开了。

1403
01:00:32.460 --> 01:00:34.380
Well, I have some news for Angela.
嗯，我有个消息要告诉安吉拉。

1404
01:00:35.140 --> 01:00:38.560
This power that she's had is going to go away
她一直以来拥有的那种权力就要消失了，

1405
01:00:38.560 --> 01:00:43.200
because Michael, Pam, and Ryan get their jobs back.
因为迈克尔、帕姆和瑞安要官复原职了。

1406
01:00:43.460 --> 01:00:43.980
Yep.
没错。

1407
01:00:44.240 --> 01:00:45.400
That's the buyout.
这就是收购协议。

1408
01:00:45.560 --> 01:00:47.800
The buyout is that they are all now reemployed
收购协议就是他们现在都被邓德·米夫林重新雇佣了，我猜，查尔斯被解雇了吗？

1409
01:00:47.800 --> 01:00:52.760
by Dunder Mifflin, and I guess, is Charles fired?
这一点我一直没搞清楚。

1410
01:00:52.760 --> 01:00:54.640
That was never clear to me.
不，我觉得他没被解雇。

1411
01:00:54.800 --> 01:00:56.060
No, I don't think he was fired.
他还会出现在公司野餐会上。

1412
01:00:56.120 --> 01:00:58.480
He's gonna show up in company picnic again.
是啊，不，据我理解，

1413
01:00:58.640 --> 01:01:00.060
Yeah, no, my understanding,
而且我重读了剧本。

1414
01:01:00.060 --> 01:01:01.440
and I reread the script.
我推断的情况是，

1415
01:01:01.620 --> 01:01:03.820
So sort of what I inferred is that
他只是被调职了。

1416
01:01:03.820 --> 01:01:05.640
he's just getting reassigned.
嗯，显然他会离开斯克兰顿分部。

1417
01:01:05.860 --> 01:01:08.460
Well, he's gonna be out of Scranton, obviously.
但最初，迈克尔说，我要他被解雇。

1418
01:01:09.200 --> 01:01:11.880
But originally, Michael says, I want him fired.
大卫说，迈克尔，我不会那么做的。

1419
01:01:12.040 --> 01:01:13.720
